{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-223499","model_call":96,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ twitter \"advertising revenue plunging\" (+ \"user growth problem\" \"monthly active users\" advertisers))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ twitter \"advertising revenue plunging\" (+ \"user growth problem\" \"monthly active users\" advertisers))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_558386156#3_1321977782","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3186","rank":1,"snippet":"Is Missing Source: American Press Institute You Can Follow Trump Tweets Without an Account Inadequate Information for Advertisers \" , \"segment\": \"With the presidential election and Donald Trump tweeting multiple times a day, some expected a surge in Twitter's user count or a \\\"Trump bump,\\\" but it took until the first quarter on 2017 for it to materialize. Regardless, the company's revenue fell last quarter for the first time since its IPO, with <cover>advertising revenue plunging 11%. Much of the commentariat has rued the fact that such a big feature of the American cultural landscape is failing when it comes to the bottom line. Twitter's Growing Pains Twitter has a major user growth problem, </cover>a measure of an Internet business advertisers pay close attention to. Its monthly active users (MAUs) increased 20% year-over-year in Q4 2014, 6% in Q4 2015 and only 4% in Q4 2016. Its user growth bounced back to 6% in Q1 2017, a jump Twitter attributed to more interest in political news and technical changes on the site. However, as an analyst at Wedbush Securities said, \"One quarter isn’t a trend, so let’s see if ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_558386156#3_1321977782","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":321},"model_calls":96,"document_judgments":49,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
