{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-223499","model_call":98,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ twitter \"ad targeting\" facebook advertisers (+ revenue advertising data))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ twitter \"ad targeting\" facebook advertisers (+ revenue advertising data))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_558386156#13_1321995671","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3188","rank":1,"snippet":"spending for the first time last year. It now makes up 37% of total ad spending. “ Digital advertising is not only pulling dollars from traditional media, but it’s also creating new advertising opportunities at the local and national level,” said eMarketer forecasting analyst Martín Utreras. However, social marketers admit that ROI is difficult to estimate. In this scenario, the company that offers you the best <cover>ad targeting, useful metrics and the biggest audience is king. Facebook dominates the social ad spending market and this is despite it miscalculating data in the past. In its latest earnings press release, Twitter admitted that aside from user growth problems, escalating competition for digital advertising spending and efforts to re-evaluate its revenue product feature portfolio will impact revenue growth. The company is looking to encourage advertisers </cover>to buy more expensive video ads in conjunction with its livestreaming TV push. Ad engagement grew 151% year over year in the last quarter thanks to video ad impressions. But is there more it could do to attract and please advertisers?\" , \"start_char\": 7427.000000 , \"title\": \"Why Twitter's Problems Aren't Going Away (","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_558386156#13_1321995671","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":91},"model_calls":98,"document_judgments":49,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-223499","model_call":98,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3188"},"model_calls":98,"document_judgments":49,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-223499","model_call":98,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3188"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q3188"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_501737412#3_1079143393","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3188","rank":2,"snippet":"Ads are for conversion. They actually used to have a lead gen tool, but retired it and haven’t brought it back. Interestingly enough, they added a Lead Gen functionality to SlideShare this summer. Maybe there’s hope yet? No Custom Audiences or Remarketing = Not Awesome Targeting The recent batch of updates doesn’t address the lack of <cover>ad targeting options available to advertisers in the LinkedIn self-service ad platform. Both Twitter and Facebook Ads have the ability to target existing customers and lists. To date, there’s no way to upload a defined audience using emails or phone numbers to the LinkedIn Self-Service ad platform, and then target them with ads tailored for what you already know about those people. And remarketing? It’s epic on Twitter, but on LinkedIn… fuggedaboutit. ( Note that LinkedIn offers a separate advertising </cover>product for large advertisers called Lead Accelerator, which does support remarketing.)\" , \"start_char\": 2610.000000 , \"title\": \"LinkedIn Ads Rolls Out New Campaign Management Tool (And I Love It) | WordStream\" , \"url\": \"https://smallbiztrends.com/2015/09/new-linkedin-campaign-manager.html\"","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_558386156#13_1321995671","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":9},"model_calls":98,"document_judgments":49,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
